From: MakerOS <noreply@makeros>
Subject: [PATCH] core: merge request controls instead of overwriting them

libcamera 0.7 no longer allows replacing Request::controls() wholesale
("Overwriting Request::controls() is not allowed" -> abort). Merge the
pending controls into the request's own list, as upstream rpicam-apps
v1.11.1 does.

Upstream: https://github.com/raspberrypi/rpicam-apps/compare/v1.11.0...v1.11.1
---
--- a/core/rpicam_app.cpp
+++ b/core/rpicam_app.cpp
@@ -894,7 +894,8 @@
 
 	{
 		std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(control_mutex_);
-		request->controls() = std::move(controls_);
+		request->controls().merge(controls_, ControlList::MergePolicy::OverwriteExisting);
+		controls_.clear();
 	}
 
 	if (camera_->queueRequest(request) < 0)
